      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Ankle sprains, burns, cuts and lacerated wounds, ingrowing toenail - topics, that are common in the general practitioner's office. Just peanuts? If they are correctly treated, yes, maybe. But if poorly diagnosed and badly treated they turn out to be troublesome for the patient and the doctor - a real \"pain in the neck\"! Therefore competent treatment is mandatory, also for these \"peanuts\"!"},
